    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><strong>Tier 3 — Ironbound Ascendants</strong></p><p><strong>“Height is not terrain. It is policy.”</strong></p><p>Ironbound Ascendants make strongholds out of bad footing and turn cliffs into arguments. They understand supply lines, choke valleys, and the spiritual value of making your enemies climb tired. If a mountain matters, they intend to own the meaning of it.</p><p><em>You’ve learned how to make distance and gravity part of the argument.</em></p><ul><li><strong>Tactical:</strong> You reroll the lowest die on checks made to climb, endure thin air or treacherous footing, and establish or contest a fortified high-ground position.</li><li><strong>Strategic:</strong> Enemy movement through your controlled Mountains/Highlands is less flexible and easier to predict.</li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
